.TH AK980 1 "2026-10-29" "ak980 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ak980 \- configure the AJAZZ AK980 V2 keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ak980
.RI [ command ] " " [ options ]
.br
.B ak980-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ak980
sets up the AJAZZ AK980 V2 keyboard on Linux: the clock and animations of its 1.14\(dq screen,
the keyboard's lighting effects and per-key colours, lighting effects computed on the PC, key
remapping on the base and Fn layers, macros, profiles and keyboard options.
Without a command it opens the app window.
.PP
Settings that the keyboard stores need the USB cable. Through the 2.4 GHz dongle the keyboard
only accepts the clock and reports its battery level.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui \fR[\fB\-\-tray\fR]
Open the app window, optionally hidden in the tray.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR | \fB\-\-waybar\fR]
Connection, battery level, active profile and whether the background agent runs.
\fB\-\-json\fR prints it for scripts, with the battery estimate; \fB\-\-waybar\fR as a Waybar
custom module with \fBreturn\-type json\fR reads it.
.TP
.B battery \fR[\fB\-\-show on\fR|\fBoff\fR] [\fB\-\-reset\fR]
What the agent has learned from whole cycles over 2.4 GHz: how long a full charge lasts, how long
charging takes, the battery's condition against the first measured charge, and how long the charge
lasts now. \fB\-\-show on\fR shows the estimates in the window and in \fBstatus\fR;
\fB\-\-reset\fR forgets the measured cycles.
.TP
.B time \fR[\fB\-\-slot \fIN\fR] | \fB\-\-auto \fIhourly|daily|weekly|manual\fR
Set the screen clock to the system time. Setting it also switches the screen to its clock page.
With \fB\-\-auto\fR, choose how often the agent sets it on its own (default weekly; a new time
zone is followed at once).
.TP
.B agent \fR[\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-\-interval \fIMIN\fR]
Run the background agent. It sets the clock as \fBtime \-\-auto\fR says and when the time zone
changes; streams PC lighting effects; switches profiles for programs; runs launcher keys and
reminders. With \fB\-\-system\fR it only keeps the clock and reads
\fI/etc/ak980/agent.conf\fR.
.TP
.B lcd \fIFILE\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Upload a GIF, an image or a folder of numbered frames to the screen (up to 140 frames).
Options: \fB\-\-fit\fR fit|fill|stretch, \fB\-\-rotate\fR 0|90|180|270, \fB\-\-zoom\fR,
\fB\-\-pan\fR \fIX,Y\fR, \fB\-\-sharp\fR, \fB\-\-tone\fR natural|grey|sepia|negative, \fB\-\-hue\fR,
\fB\-\-order\fR forward|backward|bounce, \fB\-\-speed\fR, \fB\-\-delay\fR, \fB\-\-step\fR,
\fB\-\-trim\-start\fR, \fB\-\-trim\-end\fR, \fB\-\-text\fR, \fB\-\-scroll\fR [\fIPX\fR] (running text),
\fB\-\-outline\fR, \fB\-\-preview\fR \fIOUT.gif\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR. Every upload is also kept in \fI~/.local/share/ak980/history\fR.
.TP
.B effects
List the keyboard's lighting effects and the PC effects.
.TP
.B light \fR[\fIEFFECT\fR] [\fB\-\-color \fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-\-rainbow on|off\fR] [\fB\-\-brightness \fI0..5\fR] [\fB\-\-speed \fI0..5\fR] [\fB\-\-direction \fI0..3\fR] [\fB\-\-balance \fIR,G,B\fR]
Set a lighting effect that runs in the keyboard. \fB\-\-balance\fR sets the white balance in percent
(40 to 100 each) for every colour sent from now on: white looks pink on the AK980 V2, and 78,100,95
evened it out on one.
.TP
.B fx \fR[\fIEFFECT\fR] [\fIsetting\fB=\fIvalue\fR ...] [\fB\-\-brightness \fI0..100\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR]
Choose a PC lighting effect (wave, drift, breath, starlight, reactive, fire, spectrum, pulse).
The agent or the app streams it to the keyboard.
.TP
.B custom \fR[\fB\-\-all \fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-\-key \fIKEY\fB=\fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-\-wasd \fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\fR]
Store per-key colours in the keyboard.
.TP
.B options \fR[\fB\-\-win\-lock\fR] [\fB\-\-alt\-tab\-lock\fR] [\fB\-\-alt\-f4\-lock\fR] [\fB\-\-fn\-toggle\fR] [\fB\-\-sleep \fI0..3\fR] [\fB\-\-response \fI1..5\fR]
Keyboard options; each switch takes on or off.
.TP
.B keys
Key names accepted by \fBremap\fR and \fBcustom\fR.
.TP
.B remap \fIKEY ACTION\fR [\fB\-\-fn\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\fR] | \fB\-\-reset\fR | \fB\-\-list\fR
Remap a key. ACTION is one of: default, off, key:ctrl+shift+A, mouse:left|right|middle|double|btn4|btn5|wheelup|wheeldown,
media:play|next|prev|volup|voldown|mute|calc|..., macro:N[:once|repeat:K|toggle|hold|click], multi:A,B,C.
.TP
.B remind list|add \fIHH:MM TEXT\fB|rm \fIN\fB|try \fR[\fIEFFECT\fR]
Reminders: at the time, a notification once and the keys calling for attention. \fBadd\fR takes
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI1,2,3\fR (Sunday = 0), \fB\-\-minutes\fR, \fB\-\-effect\fR
flash|pulse|sweep|alternate|rainbow, \fB\-\-color\fR and \fB\-\-screen\fR (the text on the screen
too; that writes the screen twice, the text and the last animation again). \fBtry\fR plays an effect
for a few seconds.
.TP
.B macro list|add \fINAME SPEC\fB|rm \fIN\fB|clear|upload
Manage macros. SPEC is text:\fITEXT\fR, combo:\fIctrl+alt+del\fR or steps:down:A,wait:50,up:A,click:left.
.TP
.B launch \fIKEY COMMAND\fR | \fB\-\-rm \fIKEY\fR | \fB\-\-list\fR
Make one of F13\(enF24 run a program or open a link; send that key from a remapped key.
.TP
.B profile list|use \fINAME\fB|apply|new \fINAME\fB [\-\-copy]|rm \fINAME\fB|rename \fIOLD NEW\fB|export \fINAME FILE\fB|import \fIFILE
Manage profiles. \fBuse\fR switches and sends the profile to the keyboard.
.TP
.B auto on|off|list|add \fIPROCESS PROFILE\fB|rm \fIPROCESS\fB|default \fR[\fIPROFILE\fR]
Switch profiles automatically while a program runs. \fBdefault\fR names the profile to use
after the program exits; without one, the profile that was on before comes back.
.TP
.B service list|enable \fIID\fB|disable \fIID
Start the agent automatically. IDs: session (XDG autostart), systemd-user, dinit-user,
runit-user, system-systemd, system-openrc, system-dinit, system-runit, system-s6.
dinit-user and runit-user use the user's own dinit or runsvdir, whether turnstile or userspawn
starts it. Every service description is checked (dinit with \fBdinit-check\fR) before it is
written, and only the init system's own tool enables it. A system service only starts a program
that only root can change; the system agent gives up root for \fBnobody\fR with the \fBinput\fR group.
.TP
.B setup
Install the udev rule that lets your user access the keyboard (asks for your password).
It also replaces an older copy left in /etc/udev/rules.d, such as the one 0.0.1 wrote.
.TP
.B apply
Send the active profile and the time to the keyboard.
.TP
.B link \fR[\fB\-n \fIlines\fR]
Print the 2.4 GHz link record: when the keyboard answered over the receiver, when it stopped and
when it switched between the cable and the receiver.
.TP
.B reconnect
Make the PC drop the 2.4 GHz receiver and find it again, as if it had been plugged in anew (asks for
your password). For keys that stop arriving over 2.4 GHz.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-lang \fRauto|en|uk
Interface language.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ak980/config.json
Profiles and settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ak980/history/
Copies of every animation uploaded to the screen.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ak980/link.log
The 2.4 GHz link record the agent keeps (see \fBlink\fR).
.TP
.I /etc/ak980/agent.conf
Settings of the system service (clock_slot, sync_interval_min).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-ajazz-ak980.rules
Access rule: opens the interfaces the app uses and keeps the ones that carry keystrokes root-only.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ak980 time
ak980 lcd ~/Pictures/cat.gif \-\-fit fill
ak980 fx spectrum palette=fire sensitivity=70
ak980 remap CapsLock key:ctrl
ak980 macro add "Hello" "text:Hello, world!" && ak980 remap F12 macro:0
ak980 auto add cs2 Gaming && ak980 auto on
ak980 service enable dinit\-user
.fi
.SH NOTES
Unofficial software, not affiliated with AJAZZ. Writing to a key layer replaces the whole layer.
The keyboard cannot give an uploaded animation back, which is why every upload is kept.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/yellowhearth1/ajazz\-ak980\-v2\-linux
